\title{tidymail: A Tidy, Backend-Independent Interface for Email}
\description{
Email as data in R. Messages are built with 'build_msg()' and sent with 'send_mail()' over SMTP using 'blastula'. Mailboxes are read with 'fetch_mail()' over IMAP using 'mRpostman' and returned as tibbles that can be filtered, arranged and mutated like any data frame. Attachments are listed in the result and saved with 'download_attachments()'. Passwords are kept in the system keychain or read from environment variables, never stored in the objects.
